      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T18:40:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Update from live hardware testing: we measured `22.0 KB/s` on random data (`95.28s` for 2 MB, 100% SHA-256 match) and `97.7 KB/s` on sparse/`ext2` data (`21.46s` for 2 MB).\n\nTracing `board/servo_v4p1/usb_bridge.c` shows why random-data throughput is `22.0 KB/s` rather than ~`78 KB/s`: `bridge_to_usart4` has `QUEUE_SIZE \u003d 128` (`usb_bridge.c:42`), while each 64-byte USB chunk encodes to a `68-byte` COBS wire frame (`0x00` + header + 64B + CRC8 + `0x00`). Because `2 * 68 \u003d 136 \u003e 128`, only ONE 68-byte frame fits in `bridge_to_usart4` at a time, so every second 64B USB packet hits `cobs_TryQueuePacket() \u003d\u003d 0` and waits on `hook_call_deferred(\u0026usb_bridge_process_data, 1 * MSEC)`. Since `RO` still has `240 bytes` of free RAM, bumping `bridge_to_usart4` from `128` to `192` bytes (using 64 B of the 240 B free RAM) will allow two 68-byte frames to queue back-to-back without waiting on the 1ms deferred timer. Resolving this thread as non-blocking!",
      "parentUuid": "697243a4_ada11dac",
      "revId": "80b5532ccc31156bf4be4b2154dd9df12bc6a59e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
